  <section class="card" id="english">
    <h1>NumUp: Numbers Over Your Head – Privacy Policy</h1>

    <p class="date">
      Effective: September 8, 2026<br>
      Last Updated: September 20, 2026
    </p>

    <p class="company">
      Provider: AKI Cyber Applications LLC
    </p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled in
      “NumUp: Numbers Over Your Head” (“the App”).
    </p>

    <p>
      AKI Cyber Applications LLC (“Provider”) respects user privacy
      and provides the App in accordance with this policy.
    </p>


    <h2>1. Information Handled by the App</h2>

    <p>
      The App handles the following information on your device
      only as necessary to provide its features.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Camera images:</strong>
        Used to detect people, dogs, and cats and to create
        result images with numbers overlaid.
        Images are analyzed on the device.
        Captured images and analysis results are not sent
        to the Provider's servers.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Photo library or selected folder:</strong>
        Used to save result images to the standard photo library
        or a folder selected by the user.
        The App does not collect other files from the destination
        or send them to the Provider.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>Text entered by the user:</strong>
        The meaning entered for the numbers is used on the result screen
        and in images that are saved or shared.
        This text is not sent to the Provider's servers.
      </li>

      <li>
        <strong>App settings:</strong>
        The selected language and the reference information and display name
        of the selected save-location folder are stored on the device.
      </li>
    </ul>


    <h2>2. Technical Information Handled by Google ML Kit</h2>

    <p>
      The App uses Google ML Kit to detect human faces on the device.
      According to Google, input images and detection results
      are not sent to Google servers.
    </p>

    <p>
      ML Kit may contact Google servers to receive bug fixes,
      model updates, hardware accelerator compatibility information,
      and similar technical information.
    </p>

    <p>
      For diagnostics and usage analytics, ML Kit may also send
      device and app information, a per-installation identifier,
      performance information, API configuration, input and output sizes,
      feature versions, event types, error codes, and similar technical data
      to Google.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google states that this information is encrypted in transit
      and is not shared with third parties.
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        ML Kit Terms &amp; Privacy:
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms">
          https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms
        </a>
      </li>

      <li>
        Google Privacy Policy:
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">
          https://policies.google.com/privacy
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>


    <h2>3. Advertising with Google AdMob</h2>

    <p>
      The App displays Google AdMob banner advertisements on the menu screen
      and interstitial advertisements before opening the camera screen.
    </p>

    <p>
      For advertising, measurement, and fraud prevention,
      the advertising SDK may collect IP addresses, device identifiers,
      app and advertisement interactions, diagnostic information,
      and similar data, and may transmit or share such information
      with Google and other relevant service providers.
    </p>

    <p>
      IP addresses may be used to estimate an approximate location.
    </p>

    <p>
      The App does not provide camera images or text entered by the user
      to the advertising SDK.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where required, an advertising consent form is displayed.
      When applicable, users may change their choices through
      “Ad privacy choices” in the App's Settings screen.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google's advertising privacy information:
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">
        https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads
      </a>
    </p>


    <h2>4. Purposes of Use</h2>

    <p>Information is handled only for the following purposes:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Taking photos and detecting people, dogs, and cats</li>
      <li>Displaying numbers and text</li>
      <li>Creating and saving result images</li>
      <li>Sharing result images with an app selected by the user</li>
      <li>Maintaining language and save-location settings</li>
      <li>ML Kit diagnostics, maintenance, performance improvement, and abuse detection</li>
      <li>AdMob advertising, measurement, and fraud prevention</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>5. Transmission and Sharing with Third Parties</h2>

    <p>
      The Provider does not collect, sell, or provide the user's
      captured images, entered text, or App settings to third parties
      through the App.
    </p>

    <p>
      Information may nevertheless be transferred to an external service
      based on the user's actions or device settings in the following cases:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        When the Share button is used, the result image and hashtags
        are passed to the social media or other app selected by the user.
        That service's terms and privacy policy then apply.
      </li>

      <li>
        If Google Photos, iCloud Photos, iCloud Drive,
        or another cloud destination is selected,
        result images may be stored or synchronized by that service.
      </li>

      <li>
        Google ML Kit may send Google the technical information
        described in Section 2.
      </li>

      <li>
        Google AdMob may transmit or share the advertising-related
        information described in Section 3 with Google
        and other relevant service providers.
      </li>
    </ul>


    <h2>6. Device Permissions</h2>

    <p>
      The App requests camera permission to use the camera,
      and either photo access or access to a folder selected by the user
      to save result images.
    </p>

    <p>
      These permissions can be revoked at any time through
      the device's settings.
      Features that require a denied permission will not be available.
    </p>

    <p>
      The App does not access the microphone, precise location,
      or contacts.
    </p>


    <h2>7. Retention and Deletion</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        Temporary files used for capture and image generation
        are processed in temporary storage on the device
        and are deleted after processing or are subject to cleanup
        by the operating system.
      </li>

      <li>
        Result images saved to the photo library or a selected folder
        remain until the user deletes them using a photo
        or file-management application.
        Images stored or synchronized in a cloud service may also
        need to be deleted from that service separately.
      </li>

      <li>
        Language settings and the selected folder's reference information
        and display name remain on the device until they are changed,
        the App's data is cleared, or the App is uninstalled.
      </li>

      <li>
        Technical information sent by ML Kit is retained and deleted
        in accordance with Google's Privacy Policy.
      </li>

      <li>
        Advertising-related information transmitted or shared by Google AdMob
        is retained and deleted in accordance with the privacy policies
        of Google and other applicable service providers.
      </li>
    </ul>


    <h2>8. Security</h2>

    <p>
      The Provider takes reasonable measures to protect information
      handled by the App, including avoiding unnecessary external
      transmissions and using the device's permission system.
    </p>

    <p>
      Services selected by the user for sharing or cloud synchronization
      are governed by their own security and privacy practices.
    </p>


    <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      The App does not include a mechanism intended for the Provider
      to knowingly collect children's personal information.
    </p>

    <p>
      Parents and guardians should appropriately manage device permissions,
      photo destinations, and sharing destinations.
    </p>


    <h2>10. Changes to This Policy</h2>

    <p>
      This policy may be updated when the App's features,
      SDKs, applicable laws, or app-store requirements change.
    </p>

    <p>
      Material changes will be announced through the App,
      its store listing, or another appropriate method.
    </p>


    <h2>11. Contact</h2>

    <p>
      For questions regarding this Privacy Policy or
      the App's handling of information,
      please use the developer contact information listed
      on the App's App Store or Google Play page.
    </p>

